  <script type="application/json" data-target="react-app.embeddedData">{"payload":{"commit":{"oid":"c691d821bfab9bef5bf2a2c3f623402ac32b64d3","url":"/WICG/webcomponents/commit/c691d821bfab9bef5bf2a2c3f623402ac32b64d3","authoredDate":"2015-04-30T10:47:52.000-07:00","committedDate":"2015-04-30T10:47:52.000-07:00","shortMessage":null,"shortMessageMarkdown":"\u003cdiv\u003eAdd \u003ccode\u003eproposals\u003c/code\u003e directory.\u003c/div\u003e","shortMessageMarkdownLink":null,"bodyMessageHtml":"This is a directory where we store all of in-progres proposals, summaries of work, and other documentation.\nThese documents were originally created on the wiki, but wiki does not have the a robust fork/PR system,\nso we'll manage these manually just as part of the main repo.","authors":[{"login":"dglazkov","displayName":"Dimitri Glazkov","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1934?v=4","path":"/dglazkov","profileName":"Dimitri Glazkov","isGitHub":false}],"committerAttribution":false,"committer":{"login":"dglazkov","displayName":"Dimitri Glazkov","avatarUrl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1934?v=4","path":"/dglazkov","profileName":"Dimitri Glazkov","isGitHub":false},"pusher":null,"pushedDate":null,"parents":["9fcd8e703a6bf6d91c56efa9c2eda8bbf58f8a86"],"globalRelayId":"MDY6Q29tbWl0MTQyOTEwNDA6YzY5MWQ4MjFiZmFiOWJlZjViZjJhMmMzZjYyMzQwMmFjMzJiNjRkMw==","sha1":"9fcd8e703a6bf6d91c56efa9c2eda8bbf58f8a86","sha2":"c691d821bfab9bef5bf2a2c3f623402ac32b64d3"},"currentUser":null,"repo":{"id":14291040,"defaultBranch":"gh-pages","name":"webcomponents","ownerLogin":"WICG","currentUserCanPush":false,"isFork":false,"isEmpty":false,"createdAt":"2013-11-11T04:00:30.000Z","ownerAvatar":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13145324?v=4","public":true,"private":false,"isOrgOwned":true},"diffEntryData":[{"diffLines":[{"type":"HUNK","blobLineNumber":0,"text":"@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@","html":"@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":0,"left":null,"right":0},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":1,"text":"+###### Prepared by Travis Leithead and Arron Eicholz","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e###### \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003ePrepared by Travis Leithead and Arron Eicholz\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":1,"left":null,"right":1},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":2,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":2,"left":null,"right":2},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":3,"text":"+*Note: Parts of the below proposal (specifically the Worker-like JS global singleton) are based on a previous proposal by Elliott Sprehn: [DOMWorker](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1V7ci1-lBTY6AJxgN99aCMwjZKCjKv1v3y_7WLtcgM00/edit?pli=1)*","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003eNote: Parts of the below proposal (specifically the Worker-like JS global singleton) are based on a previous proposal by Elliott Sprehn: \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eDOMWorker\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-corl\"\u003ehttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1V7ci1-lBTY6AJxgN99aCMwjZKCjKv1v3y_7WLtcgM00/edit?pli=1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":3,"left":null,"right":3},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":4,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":4,"left":null,"right":4},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":5,"text":"+See also, Apple's proposal for solving the same use cases but using a 2-step creation/application process: https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/wiki/Isolated-Imports-Proposal. ","html":"+See also, Apple\u0026#39;s proposal for solving the same use cases but using a 2-step creation/application process: \u003cspan class=\"pl-corl\"\u003ehttps://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/wiki/Isolated-Imports-Proposal\u003c/span\u003e. ","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":5,"left":null,"right":5},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":6,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":6,"left":null,"right":6},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":7,"text":"+# Concept","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e# \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eConcept\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":7,"left":null,"right":7},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":8,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":8,"left":null,"right":8},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":9,"text":"+Cross-origin web components are a type of web component that fulfills the requirement for confinement in the Facebook +1 button [use-case](https://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/Component_Model_Use_Cases). Rather than establishing confinement at the shadow DOM boundary as done in the previous proposal, confinement is obtained through the establishment of a cross-origin custom element (thus use of shadow DOM in the confined component is an optional feature).","html":"+Cross-origin web components are a type of web component that fulfills the requirement for confinement in the Facebook +1 button \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003euse-case\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-corl\"\u003ehttps://wiki.whatwg.org/wiki/Component_Model_Use_Cases\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e. Rather than establishing confinement at the shadow DOM boundary as done in the previous proposal, confinement is obtained through the establishment of a cross-origin custom element (thus use of shadow DOM in the confined component is an optional feature).","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":9,"left":null,"right":9},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":10,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":10,"left":null,"right":10},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":11,"text":"+Confined components are currently handled by iframes, which additionally require another \"agent\" script to be loaded directly in the host. The agent facilitates the communication with the iframe content (via `postMessage`). Loading the additional agent is inconvenient and also requires trusting it not to overstep it's described behavior. Furthermore, iframes are also inefficient in that each new \"component\" instance comes with a new isolated script environment.","html":"+Confined components are currently handled by iframes, which additionally require another \u0026quot;agent\u0026quot; script to be loaded directly in the host. The agent facilitates the communication with the iframe content (via \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003epostMessage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e). Loading the additional agent is inconvenient and also requires trusting it not to overstep it\u0026#39;s described behavior. Furthermore, iframes are also inefficient in that each new \u0026quot;component\u0026quot; instance comes with a new isolated script environment.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":11,"left":null,"right":11},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":12,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":12,"left":null,"right":12},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":13,"text":"+When defining a component using custom elements, a custom element prototype is provided which is used as the \"template\" from which new instances of the custom element are bound and inherit functionality. In a cross-origin component, the boundary of confinement must include a prototype object as well as any instances created from it--necessitating a single JavaScript global environment in order to be most efficient (versus a global environment per custom element instance).","html":"+When defining a component using custom elements, a custom element prototype is provided which is used as the \u0026quot;template\u0026quot; from which new instances of the custom element are bound and inherit functionality. In a cross-origin component, the boundary of confinement must include a prototype object as well as any instances created from it--necessitating a single JavaScript global environment in order to be most efficient (versus a global environment per custom element instance).","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":13,"left":null,"right":13},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":14,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":14,"left":null,"right":14},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":15,"text":"+*Note: the words 'confinement/confined' and 'isolated' are used interchangeably to mean the same thing. Also, the terms \"outside\" DOM and \"inside\" DOM are from the perspective of the isolated component (i.e., outside the component, and inside the component).*","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003eNote: the words \u0026#39;confinement/confined\u0026#39; and \u0026#39;isolated\u0026#39; are used interchangeably to mean the same thing. Also, the terms \u0026quot;outside\u0026quot; DOM and \u0026quot;inside\u0026quot; DOM are from the perspective of the isolated component (i.e., outside the component, and inside the component).\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":15,"left":null,"right":15},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":16,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":16,"left":null,"right":16},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":17,"text":"+# Proposal","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e# \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eProposal\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":17,"left":null,"right":17},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":18,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":18,"left":null,"right":18},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":19,"text":"+In this proposed design, a custom element may be optionally defined by a 3rd party URL and provide safe [curated] interaction with the host environment. Several notable design considerations include:","html":"+In this proposed design, a custom element may be optionally defined by a 3rd party URL and provide safe \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003ecurated\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e interaction with the host environment. Several notable design considerations include:","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":19,"left":null,"right":19},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":20,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":20,"left":null,"right":20},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":21,"text":"+1. Only one isolated JavaScript global environment is created in order to service any/all custom element instances including their shared prototype functionality (no unnecessary duplication of resources). If shadow DOM usage is desired, it can be attached using the same code-patterns as when the custom element is not cross-origin.","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e Only one isolated JavaScript global environment is created in order to service any/all custom element instances including their shared prototype functionality (no unnecessary duplication of resources). If shadow DOM usage is desired, it can be attached using the same code-patterns as when the custom element is not cross-origin.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":21,"left":null,"right":21},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":22,"text":"+2. No corresponding \"agent\" is necessary in the outer DOM in order to provide the interaction APIs to communicate with the isolated JavaScript environment on the inside.","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e No corresponding \u0026quot;agent\u0026quot; is necessary in the outer DOM in order to provide the interaction APIs to communicate with the isolated JavaScript environment on the inside.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":22,"left":null,"right":22},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":23,"text":"+3. The provided isolation is not dependent on Shadow DOM--shadow DOM is complementary. Like the current distinction between custom elements and shadow DOM, cross-origin custom elements is independent of shadow dom.","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e The provided isolation is not dependent on Shadow DOM--shadow DOM is complementary. Like the current distinction between custom elements and shadow DOM, cross-origin custom elements is independent of shadow dom.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":23,"left":null,"right":23},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":24,"text":"+4. The cross-origin custom element imperative API is trivially adapted/shimmed to a declarative model (just saying :))","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e The cross-origin custom element imperative API is trivially adapted/shimmed to a declarative model (just saying :))","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":24,"left":null,"right":24},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":25,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":25,"left":null,"right":25},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":26,"text":"+## How does it work?","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e## \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eHow does it work?\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":26,"left":null,"right":26},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":27,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":27,"left":null,"right":27},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":28,"text":"+In the \"outside\" DOM:","html":"+In the \u0026quot;outside\u0026quot; DOM:","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":28,"left"