the constructor function (or via the parser) and they will automatically inherit from the specified prototype (if provided). The \"magic\" of the provided url causes an API and element behavior to be asynchronously bound to the specified prototype and instances with its implementation hidden in an isolated scripting environment. Step-by-step:","html":"+That\u0026#39;s it. The outside DOM may create new element instances given the constructor function (or via the parser) and they will automatically inherit from the specified prototype (if provided). The \u0026quot;magic\u0026quot; of the provided url causes an API and element behavior to be asynchronously bound to the specified prototype and instances with its implementation hidden in an isolated scripting environment. Step-by-step:","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":44,"left":null,"right":44},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":45,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":45,"left":null,"right":45},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":46,"text":"+1. The url refers to an HTML file whose script defines the custom element's prototype behavior, as well as monitoring the instance creation logic and attribute change notifications--all contained within a single new JS global scope that is fully isolated from the outside DOM.","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e The url refers to an HTML file whose script defines the custom element\u0026#39;s prototype behavior, as well as monitoring the instance creation logic and attribute change notifications--all contained within a single new JS global scope that is fully isolated from the outside DOM.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":46,"left":null,"right":46},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":47,"text":"+  * Note: the parsed HTML of the cross-origin custom element is available via a document but is not rendered. Rendering the document would require associating it with a particular element which may not have happened yet. The URL is unrestricted--same-origin, cross-origin, it doesn't matter.","html":"+  \u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e Note: the parsed HTML of the cross-origin custom element is available via a document but is not rendered. Rendering the document would require associating it with a particular element which may not have happened yet. The URL is unrestricted--same-origin, cross-origin, it doesn\u0026#39;t matter.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":47,"left":null,"right":47},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":48,"text":"+2. The fetched HTML file is executed in the context of a new JS global object, the `CustomElementGlobalScope`.","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e The fetched HTML file is executed in the context of a new JS global object, the \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eCustomElementGlobalScope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":48,"left":null,"right":48},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":49,"text":"+3. The JavaScript in the `CustomElementGlobalScope` registers any shared APIs for the Custom Element's prototype, and adds lifecycle callbacks for the management of instances that will be created based on this prototype. Additionally, the original parsed document may be cloned for use in populating a shadow DOM for any custom element instances (optional).","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e The JavaScript in the \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eCustomElementGlobalScope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e registers any shared APIs for the Custom Element\u0026#39;s prototype, and adds lifecycle callbacks for the management of instances that will be created based on this prototype. Additionally, the original parsed document may be cloned for use in populating a shadow DOM for any custom element instances (optional).","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":49,"left":null,"right":49},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":50,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":50,"left":null,"right":50},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":51,"text":"+The script in the inner `CustomElementGlobalScope` interacts with the outer environment through three mechanisms: via events (both native user agent and self-synthesized), through APIs it causes to be created on the custom element's prototype object, and by way of the attributes of custom element instances.","html":"+The script in the inner \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eCustomElementGlobalScope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e interacts with the outer environment through three mechanisms: via events (both native user agent and self-synthesized), through APIs it causes to be created on the custom element\u0026#39;s prototype object, and by way of the attributes of custom element instances.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":51,"left":null,"right":51},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":52,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":52,"left":null,"right":52},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":53,"text":"+### Events","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e### \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003eEvents\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":53,"left":null,"right":53},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":54,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":54,"left":null,"right":54},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":55,"text":"+Without a shadow DOM, events fire on the cross-origin custom element instances created in the inside DOM at the end of the event model's capture phase, and at the beginning of an event's bubble phase. No events capture/bubble to the `CustomElementGlobalScope`. If shadow DOMs are attached to these inside DOM custom element instances, they behave exactly like they would behave in the outside DOM.","html":"+Without a shadow DOM, events fire on the cross-origin custom element instances created in the inside DOM at the end of the event model\u0026#39;s capture phase, and at the beginning of an event\u0026#39;s bubble phase. No events capture/bubble to the \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eCustomElementGlobalScope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e. If shadow DOMs are attached to these inside DOM custom element instances, they behave exactly like they would behave in the outside DOM.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":55,"left":null,"right":55},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":56,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":56,"left":null,"right":56},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":57,"text":"+For the purpose of isolation, a new nested event propagation is started on the inside DOM so that no data may be carried into the isolation boundary from outside DOM.","html":"+For the purpose of isolation, a new nested event propagation is started on the inside DOM so that no data may be carried into the isolation boundary from outside DOM.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":57,"left":null,"right":57},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":58,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":58,"left":null,"right":58},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":59,"text":"+Events manually dispatched to custom elements on the inside DOM build up a nested dispatch path from the outside DOM to the inside DOM just like native event dispatches. This enables the custom element to be an event source if desired. ","html":"+Events manually dispatched to custom elements on the inside DOM build up a nested dispatch path from the outside DOM to the inside DOM just like native event dispatches. This enables the custom element to be an event source if desired. ","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":59,"left":null,"right":59},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":60,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":60,"left":null,"right":60},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":61,"text":"+### Prototype API management","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-mh\"\u003e### \u003cspan class=\"pl-en\"\u003ePrototype API management\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":61,"left":null,"right":61},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":62,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":62,"left":null,"right":62},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":63,"text":"+When a cross-origin custom element is loaded, the user agent creates a mapping between the prototype supplied or created on the outside DOM with the custom element's global scope. This mapping is used to dynamically populate the prototype object provided on the outside DOM with APIs specified on the inside DOM. Note, that the custom element global scope never has direct access to the outside DOM prototype object, and the APIs that it causes to be defined on the outside prototype object are created within the realm of the outside DOM (the APIs appear to natively belong to the outside DOM).","html":"+When a cross-origin custom element is loaded, the user agent creates a mapping between the prototype supplied or created on the outside DOM with the custom element\u0026#39;s global scope. This mapping is used to dynamically populate the prototype object provided on the outside DOM with APIs specified on the inside DOM. Note, that the custom element global scope never has direct access to the outside DOM prototype object, and the APIs that it causes to be defined on the outside prototype object are created within the realm of the outside DOM (the APIs appear to natively belong to the outside DOM).","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":63,"left":null,"right":63},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":64,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":64,"left":null,"right":64},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":65,"text":"+The cross-origin custom element manages APIs on the outside prototype object using the following new methods of the custom element global scope:","html":"+The cross-origin custom element manages APIs on the outside prototype object using the following new methods of the custom element global scope:","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":65,"left":null,"right":65},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":66,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":66,"left":null,"right":66},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":67,"text":"+* `setProperty(name, property_descriptor)` - mirroring `Object.defineProperty` for property creation","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003esetProperty(name, property_descriptor)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e - mirroring \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eObject.defineProperty\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e for property creation","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":67,"left":null,"right":67},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":68,"text":"+* `setProperties(multiple_property_descriptors)` - mirroring `Object.defineProperties` for convenience","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003esetProperties(multiple_property_descriptors)\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e - mirroring \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-c1\"\u003eObject.defineProperties\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e`\u003c