n other at-rules (and vice-versa), such as \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e@\u003cspan class=\"pl-corl\"\u003edocument\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, \u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e@\u003cspan class=\"pl-corl\"\u003emedia\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e, etc., which isn’t possible if defined out of CSS itself.","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":62,"left":null,"right":62},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":63,"text":"+  * !unimportant was my initial idea that sprang to mind, but it might become tedious to add that annotation to a large set of styles...","html":"+  \u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e !unimportant was my initial idea that sprang to mind, but it might become tedious to add that annotation to a large set of styles...","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":63,"left":null,"right":63},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":64,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":64,"left":null,"right":64},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":65,"text":"+2. What does !important do in a default style declaration?","html":"+\u003cspan class=\"pl-s\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e What does !important do in a default style declaration?","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":65,"left":null,"right":65},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":66,"text":"+","html":"+","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":66,"left":null,"right":66},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":67,"text":"+  * Like in author style sheets, the !important rules promotes those declarations into another layer. This has ","html":"+  \u003cspan class=\"pl-v\"\u003e*\u003c/span\u003e Like in author style sheets, the !important rules promotes those declarations into another layer. This has ","displayNoNewLineWarning":false,"position":67,"left":null,"right":67},{"type":"ADDITION","blobLineNumber":68,"text":"+the someone odd effect of making the default !important rules more important than a normal !important decla